        <p>Doo, As a Hobby. 414,11`0.1- keeping as a hobby gives t %spoilt af pleasure and is also profitable, and a great 4(14414re hundreds of people to-day who are g (!onsiderably to their income in this way, cowpoultry keeping as a profession requires tit .o;!,,larahle experience and a love of live stoiik toacl'er to ensure success. It is not an easy kak. ta fortu i ne, and for one man who may e ,Irokillg a big income there are hundreds wl3 IP14; 4 hard task to make ends meet, and it lirofi-fabout three years before there are anyi Worth mentioning, because the necessary MO up and additions to the equipment goner-! 11Zallow the profits from the early dealings. ZtrY keeping for domestic egg supply only ~"ate.tlil° Profitable, and that is one reason why l'l'tlss4,l‘ad stock gives a better return than d"Nds. As I said before, there is always a kood'etaand in the early part of the year foro laohf,:ggs for sitting purposes, and plenty f si Will be forthcoming if a good laying !aztil; Is l worked up. Once you get a name _o 42)eiv,;_a:ords and value for money the trade will very rapidly, and that at very little se to the breeder.</p>
