        <p>-Members of the newly-formed Warringto: Motor Cycle Club were on pleasure bent a Easter Monday, when early in the morning they assembled at Victoria-square. Stockton heath. prior to ti,?ir departure for IMO The route taken was via .lester. an '</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-18_WidnesExaminer_art0059" n="art0059">
        <head>silil CYCLISTS' NOTE' BOOK</head>
        <p>silil CYCLISTS' NOTE' BOOK</p>
        <p>Fruit Blossom iu Cheshire a Charming Attraction.</p>
        <p>BY SILVER-STREET.</p>
        <p>I am surprised at tne number of folk in War- rington who do not know what the pear orchards of Cheshire are like when in bloom. That is probably because pear trees are in blos- som so early in the year. It is worth while going to Acton Bridge this or next week in order to see it. for this year promises to be a record one for both flower and fruit. From Stockton Heath Swing Bridge (fancy daubing " Northwich-road Bridge" all over it, for all the world as if the Canal Company were com- posed of Suffragettes!) to Acton Swing Bridge is 71 miles, and by turning up the hill to the right opposite the Bone Works you reach Acton, the • orchard village. No more beautiful sight can Cheshire show than its snow-laden fruit trees, and I have yet to find a Cheshire village more given up than this to fruit growing. And later on the pink blossom of the apple trees will be equally charming. From the fork at the top of the hill either road may be followed with ad vantage—the' left over Acton Bridge Station by Crowton and Kingsley to Frodsham and home, a total round of 23 miles; or the right road, down Acton Cliff to Pickering Bridge, where tea may be obtained, and home by Aston hall and Preston Brook, total 18 miles.</p>
        <p>A USEFUL CARRIER. Or perhaps we had better call it an adjunct to the carrier. I have seen all ways of carrying handbags on bicycles; some strapped on !•.”liiial under the saddle, some fastened on to the rc:tr by a strap passed round both bag and carrier, some hung on the lamp hrack .yt :it the front. ' The objection to the last plan is that the brake fitting' • rub the bag and make. it such a sight that one would as soon think of wearing a pair of patched boots as be seen carrying it off the bicycle. An old, strong leather bag may easily be fitted to the rept- so that it involves no waste of time unstrapphig it in order to get inside. Make four slits just above the bottom seam,</p>
      </div>
