        <p>As for indirect consequences, he nnP3f. while no one contends that the removal ° drink evil would solve all the social proble,°; our time, no one can examine these sociT., blems without realising that the drinking II; of our people have an unhappy praminellet all of them. He quotes Dr. Newsholme'° ment in his report of last year that draill',e; favours excessive infant mortality; and 0,7, Report of the Lunacy Commissioners that sonal addiction to alcohol had been a faet°;l 26.3 per cent, of male and 10.4 per cent. of cases of first attacks of insanity, and thal; per cent, of the male and 4 per cent. female it was the only one which o°' assigned as ;the casual agent. Mr. Wilson quotes the opinion of the director ,°_„,f National Society for the Prevention of to Children that "it is not an exaggerate% mate that 90 per cent, of the cases of nfto inquired into by the society's officers are the habits of excessive drinking on the one or both of the parents." After referrim the Report of the Divorce Commission, calls that the late Lord Gorell and the In Lord Mersey, successive Presidents of the't bate, Divorce and Admiralty Division, ho'et left on record their opinion that "if we of drink the doom of the Divorce Court 1° almost be closed."</p>
