      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-18_WidnesExaminer_art0086" n="art0086">
        <head>CHILDREN ALL LIKE ZAM-BUK.</head>
        <p>CHILDREN ALL LIKE ZAM-BUK.</p>
        <p>Unequalled for Soothing and Healing Painful</p>
        <p>Sores and Wounds.</p>
        <p>Zam-Buk has endeared itself to the bWirns because of its wonderful soothing and healing powers. Ni common ointment can do them the same good .as this pure herbal balm. Worthless Imitations should for safety's sake be rigidly avoided.</p>
        <p>ITCHING ECZEMA CURED.—For eight</p>
        <p>weexs lions M. Ford was kept away from school by eczema. "It started with blotches on her face," writes Mrs. E. Ford, of 185, Tiverton-road, Selly Oak, Birmingham. "The sore places itched very badly and Doris was in great dis- tress. Week after week passed without the eczema showing any signs of disappearing. Then I put everything aside and used Zam-Buk. This rich balm soon removed the irritable sores and left Doris's skin clear and healthy. She is back at schbol again, quite cured by Zam-Buk."</p>
        <p>POISONED KNEE FROM'A FALL• —Clifford</p>
        <p>A.—ger-77n sedhis right knee, lie pulled his stocking over the broken skin and blood poison was thus set up. " Clifford's knee swelled and got very inflamed," writes Mrs. E. R. Kemp, from Church-street, Rochester, Kent. "Painful sores broke out on Clifford's leg. Ointments and poultices failed to heal the sores, but Zam-Buk cleansed and healed my boy's leg beautifully. The new skin Zam-Buk grew is quite healthy."</p>
        <p>SAVED HER GOLDEN LOCKS.—"Our little</p>
        <p>Kathleen, aged 4, had ringworm on her head," writes Mrs. A. E. 31cOrane, 44, Queen's-road, South Farnborough, Hants. "It started with small patches of smarting and itching sores which spread across the child's scalp. When the doctor said all her beautiful hair would have to ,be cut off, we were greatly distressed. " Zam-Buk, however, saved the child's lovely hair. All inflammation and itching were soothed, and the ringworms gradually disap- neared as I persevered with Zam-Buk. Kath- leen is now completely cured and her golden locks are once more beautiful."</p>
