      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-18_WidnesExaminer_art0121" n="art0121">
        <head>BIRTHS. MARRIAGES. DEATHS.</head>
        <p>BIRTHS. MARRIAGES. DEATHS.</p>
        <p>Notices of births, marriages, and deaths, in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in the "Examiner" at the following rates :—Not exceeding 20 words, is. 6d. each; every additional seven words. 6d.</p>
        <p>Deaths. BROADITURST.—On Thursday, 16th, Mrs. William Broadhurst, late of Winwiek-road. Interment Warrington Cemetery, 2 p.m., Sunday next.</p>
        <p>DAKIN.—On Wednesday, the 15th, at the Willows, Grappenhall, Alfred Thurston Dakin, ih his 67th year. Interment at Grappenhall Church to-clay (Saturday) at 12 noon. No flowers by special request.</p>
        <p>MOUNFIELD &amp; SONS carry out Funerals 4 in town and country. Every equipment. Office: 16, Church-street. Tel. 99.</p>
