        <p>been appropriated for little girls' wear. It will I prove a formidable rival to white, which one always associates with childhood. Black and white checks are quite a craze at present for boys as well as girls, and suits and dresses of poplin, silk, and all kinds of materials are shown in this favourite plaid. Tangerine, as the shade of yellow is called, will prove a serious rival. All kinds of pretty coats and hats for children are made from a new 'lustre wool, in- terwoven with gold bronze fibre, which gives ' the wool a silky, glinting appearance. It makes pretty ties and waistcoats for men and boys. , A very remarkable wool, which, when made into a garment is brushed vigorously, is another novelty. The brushing raises a surface re- sembling fur, which is retained after washing. This wool is by no means expensive.</p>
