        <p>HIPPODROME EASTER ATTRACT!</p>
        <p>Plenty of Mirth and Fun. The holiday attractions at the Hip this week are excellent, and as usual lax_ ences have been the rule. "Navy Blue" title of .a nautical dramatic sketch presex</p>
        <p>,podi</p>
        <p>admirably by Reginald -Davia and</p>
        <p>There is plenty of excitement, but this balanced by dashes of breezy humour. Davis appears with success as Jack Mel and he is everything that a seaman shot</p>
        <p>Miss Cwenda Wren, Mr. Edmund Snell, J. Charlwood and Mr. Fred Benningti</p>
        <p>assist in the piece: Graham, described human marionette, gives a rather nove</p>
        <p>presenting by means" of marionettes an</p>
        <p>the music-- hail stage as it was 30 years ag° the one of to-day, with "stars" of both Per Vere and Neldon score a success as bale artistes, and the Gillettes create much laug with their rich comedy in The crazy....l man." A dancing turn is given by The is sons, and Baker and Balfe prove thetaself° pert xylophonists. Monty Walker is a vers Lancashire comedian, with a fund of tol humour. He has some of the best topical PI and gags heard on the stage for some time, always gets home his " laughs."</p>
        <p>A " First Visit" Week.</p>
        <p>The comedy element will be strongly denee next week at the Hippodrome, where' Kitchen and his company tops the bill. sketch "Bungle's Luck" is of the opal' variety, and for its production special 0 and scenery has had to be obtained, to sfl49! ing of the numerous costumes. There Wib full chorus, and the orchestra will be undin supervision of Mr. Dudley Powell.</p>
        <p>The first visit to the town is also announci Mabel and Cliff Diamond, in their singing (Mooing scena. The latest novelty " aerial ball match on cycles" will be presented 11 Impenial Cycle Troupe, who also are 018 their first visit to Warrington. The other t are: Billy Amstell, comedian; The Phydora their dancing and musical act; Godfrey. 11'11.i by Miss Vedo, card manipulator; and-P Clifford, character comedian. It is wort note that the entire programme is new to rington audiences, for each separate turn 0 its debut in the town on Monday. •</p>
        <p>THE PICTURE HOUSE. Au exceedingly attractive programme le provided at the Picture House next week,,/, the principal film will be "King Charles.' , picture will be shown for the latter part 0: week, whilst for the earlier days "Steel thrilling drama, will be exhibited.</p>
