        <p>Great Success of "The Younger Generatit Those who witnessed "llindle Wakes" b 5, late Stanley Houghton, anticipated sonic' exceptionally good when "The Younger Gel tion " by the same author was announce visit the Royal Court Theatre, and this : those anticipations have been more than 7, fled. "The Younger Generation" is a real study, and in it there is an abundance of and genuine humour. " The old order changeth and giveth Plll the new," and here we see the actual chen process. Narrow-minded, bigoted, Puritel parents endeavour to rule their children have been ruled—or misruled in some but the younger:generation break down sta</p>
        <p>sew</p>
        <p>the</p>
        <p>riers of mock-modesty and distrust, and traces of undue prejudice, much to the L of the "Early Victorian" grandmother, -Nen Paynes and 11. Theodore's con:wail., out all the features in the play in a stri* realistic fashion. No word of praise is VI for any member of the company, for vied RH play their parts with consummate skiu the resuit is "realism on the stage."</p>
